<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Nasi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as João Miques</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Nasi was a Portuguese-born Jewish financier and diplomat who rose to great influence at the Ottoman court under Selim II. In 1566 the sultan made him duke of Naxos and the Archipelago after deposing its last Crispo duke, and he ruled the islands through a deputy. He also sponsored Jewish resettlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberias">Tiberias</a>.</p></div>
